## Rules for Claude Code

### Rule 1 — Orient first
Call `bridge_manifest()` at the start of every session.
Never assume which domains exist.

### Rule 2 — Fetch by domain
Only fetch the domain relevant to what you are working on.
Do not load all domains at once.

| Working on                | Fetch                                                        |
|---------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| Any local component       | `bridge_get("<domain>", "<component>")`                      |
| A cross-repo contract     | `bridge_get_contract("<name>")`                              |
| Something in another repo | `bridge_get_from("<path>", "<domain>", "<component>")`       |
| Discovery                 | `bridge_list()` or `bridge_list("<domain>")`                 |

### Rule 3 — Contracts define boundaries
Read the contract for any cross-repo interaction.
Do not read another repo's internal domains unless debugging a mismatch.

### Rule 4 — Write back after implementing
After adding or changing anything described in `.context/`, update the file:
```
bridge_update("<domain>", "<component>", <content>)
```

### Rule 5 — Keep manifest current
After creating a new domain or component, patch the manifest:
```
bridge_manifest_update({ patch: { domains: { "<domain>": ["<component>"] } } })
```

